    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Denim's history traces back to the 15th-century Age of Exploration — it's said that Columbus's sails were made from this sturdy fabric. Originating in Nîmes, France, it was called 'Sergé de Nîmes,' later shortened by the English to 'denim.'",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
