      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The rugged, durable denim perfectly complements the motorcycle bag's spirit. Launched in 2001, the Le City is Balenciaga's most iconic handbag, originally designed to be 'a cool bag for girls who ride motorcycles.'",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Logo-free, its signature elements are metal studs, leather pull-tab zippers, and distressed leather. The overall look is rugged and androgynous, subverting the era's elegant mainstream aesthetic.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "text": null,
      "url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/i37ehjg/c22aeab92382ae5c.jpg",
      "full_url": "https://cdn.kynbag.com/images/i37ehjg/c22aeab92382ae5c.jpg",
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "caption",
      "text": "Then-creative director Nicolas Ghesquière with Le City handbag, 2004 ©VOGUE",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The bag retains classic motorcycle details like thimble-shaped studs, small metal corner reinforcements, and functional zip pockets. It simplifies the original embossed studs and bottom feet, preserving its iconic look while reducing weight.",
      "url": null,
      "full_url": null,
      "alt": null,
      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
